  "summary": "Audited steering-doc.md against evidence.md and, where reproducible, directly against the repo and installed packages (git log/remote/gh repo view, .gitignore, package.json absence, SDK import probe, ~/.pi/agent/settings.json and auth.json, installed pi-coding-agent 0.84.2 type declarations and docs/sdk.md, Node/agent-browser/electron-vite versions). Traced every Decision's *Enforced:* line to its choke-point name in Shape/Contracts, every Zone B behaviour-table row and every '## Not doing' bullet back to the Decision it cites, and checked the '## Not doing' preamble against its own bullets. Found two blocking issues: (1) '## Not doing' claims 'nothing refuses it at runtime' but its own next bullet says abort/steer is 'refused instead (D6)', and D6 plus the behaviour table confirm this is a real runtime refusal mechanism — a direct self-contradiction; (2) the behaviour-table row for empty/whitespace-only prompts introduces a new pane-validation rule with no basis in any Zone A Decision, mis-cited to D6 (which only covers turn concurrency) — Zone B decision leakage. Found four minor issues: two '(Contracts)' citations (D3's toPortEvent, D11's createSdkAdapter) pointing to names that exist only in Shape, not Contracts; a softer version of the Not-doing/preamble tension on the tool/thinking/compaction/retry bullet; an under-specified 'warn record' behaviour tacked onto D5 without Zone A backing; and an imprecise field name ('source' vs. the primary doc's 'sourceId') in Facts on file. All other claims — repo/git/GitHub state, SDK type surface and streaming semantics, Electron/electron-vite security prior art, Agent Browser and environment facts — were verified accurate, several independently reproduced rather than trusted from evidence.md. Findings written to fact-audit.md.",
  "verdict": "{\"blocking\": [\"'## Not doing' preamble ('Everything here is a scope fence: not built, nothing refuses it at runtime.') is directly contradicted by its own bullet 'Abort, steer, follow-up while streaming — refused instead (D6)': D6's text and the Zone B behaviour table confirm this is an active runtime refusal (single-flight guard, terminal error code:'busy'), not an absence — the same class of gap the audit brief names explicitly.\", \"Zone B behaviour-table row 'Empty or whitespace-only prompt | the pane does not call the port; no turn id, no log record | D6' introduces a new decision (client-side input validation in the pane) that is not established anywhere in Zone A (Decisions, Shape, Assumptions, Not doing, Done looks like) and is mis-cited to D6, which is solely about turn concurrency/single-flight — this is Zone B decision leakage under an unrelated Decision's name.\"], \"minor\": [\"D3's '*Enforced:* toPortEvent in the SDK adapter (Contracts)' and D11's '*Enforced:* createSdkAdapter's in-memory session construction (Contracts)' both cite '(Contracts)' but neither name appears in the Contracts section — both appear only in Shape's SDK-adapter entry, so the parenthetical pointer is wrong even though the underlying traceability rule (name appears in Shape or Contracts) is technically satisfied.\", \"'## Not doing' bullet 'Tool calls, thinking, compaction, retries in the port — dropped by the mapping (D3)' is in the same mild tension with the 'nothing refuses it at runtime' preamble as the blocking abort/steer finding, though weaker since dropping/filtering is not the same as refusing a request.\", \"Behaviour-table row on CRUCIBLE_AGENT unrecognized values adds a specific 'one warn record' logging behaviour not stated in D5's own text (only plausibly inferred by combining D5 and D8).\", \"'Facts on file' bullet says webContents console-message carries 'level and source', but evidence.md's own fetch of the primary Electron doc records the parameter as 'sourceId', not 'source' — a minor field-name imprecision.\"]}"
